### Content summary

- **Purpose** — AI judgment on focal path (hero → proof → depth) via scale, contrast, grouping, and CTA weight; complements `DET.CTA.HIERARCHY`, `DET.BUTTON.GROUP.MAX`, `DET.SECTION.HEADING`.
- **Passing / failing signals** — Actionable lists tied to KS classes (`product-landing-title`, `landing-hero-tagline`, `btn-forge`, `btn-cyan-outline`, `section-label`, `card-amber`, `breathe-static`, etc.).
- **Before example** — Failing hero with competing `h2`/`h1`/`h2`, four CTAs, stat card competing with copy, three equal `card-amber` outcome tiles.
- **After example** — Passing hero with single `product-landing-title`, primary + outline CTA + secondary link, diagram in `landing-hero-visual`, one accented outcome tile + two `breathe-static` siblings, mechanism band at lower weight.
- **Evidence and remediation** — Squint test, DOM capture, 7-step fix order with deterministic promotion path.
- **Related rules** — Links to `AI.VISUAL.HIERARCHY_CONFIDENCE` (canonical sibling), deterministic CTA/heading rules, narrative/premium/burden AI rules.

